.\" Title: vrw-purge
.\" Author: vrw contributors
.\" Manual section: 1
.\" Process this file with
.\"   groff -man -Tascii vrw-purge.1

.TH VRW\-PURGE 1 "2025" "vrw" "User Commands"

.SH NAME
vrw\-purge \- purge a retained (exited) command from the manager

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vrw
\fBpurge\fR [\fITARGET\fR] [\fB\-i\fR, \fB\-\-interactive\fR]

.SH DESCRIPTION
Purge a retained (exited) command from the vrw command manager, permanently discarding the VTTY buffer and all associated state. Only commands that have already exited (status: not alive) can be purged. Running commands cannot be purged; use \fBvrw stop-command\fR first.

When \fB\-\-retain\-on\-exit\fR is enabled (either globally or per-command), commands remain in memory after their child process exits. This allows inspection of the final output via the web UI or API. Once you are done inspecting the output, use \fBpurge\fR to free the memory.

If no target is given and exactly one exited command exists across all instances, that command is purged automatically. If multiple exited commands exist, a list is displayed with instructions to specify which one to purge.

Target matching follows a two-phase strategy:
.RS
.IP 1. 4
ID prefix match: the target matches the beginning of a command UUID.
.IP 2. 4
Name match: same three-round strategy as \fBstop-command\fR (exact, prefix on full string, prefix on name only).
.RE

.SH ARGUMENTS

.TP
.B TARGET
Command ID (or ID prefix), command name, or full "name args" string of the exited command to purge. If omitted and exactly one exited command exists, it is purged automatically.

.SH OPTIONS

.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-interactive
Present a numbered list of exited commands and let the user select
which ones to purge by typing space-separated numbers (e.g. "1 3 5").
Requires a terminal (stdin must be a TTY).

.SH EXAMPLES

.PP
Purge the only exited command (target omitted):
.RS
.PP
.nf
\fB$ vrw purge\fR
Purging only exited command: cargo build (ID abc123...)
Purged: cargo build
.fi
.RE

.PP
Purge by command ID prefix:
.RS
.PP
.nf
\fB$ vrw purge abc123\fR
Purged: cargo build
.fi
.RE

.PP
Purge by name:
.RS
.PP
.nf
\fB$ vrw purge htop\fR
Purged: htop
.fi
.RE

.PP
Equivalent curl:
.RS
.PP
.nf
curl -s -X DELETE "http://localhost:9090/api/commands/abc123"
.fi
.RE

.SH EXIT STATUS

.TP
.B 0
Command purged successfully.

.TP
.B 1
No matching exited command found, or purge request failed.

.SH SEE ALSO

.BR vrw (1),
.BR vrw\-stop\-command (1),
.BR vrw\-list (1),
.BR vrwctrl (1)
